  "weekLabel": "Week of Nov 16–20, 2026",
  "headline": "Anthropic sets $70–$78 terms for a Nov 19 Nasdaq debut, the week's only scheduled IPO",
  "summary": "Anthropic (ANT) is the only deal on Renaissance's Nov 16–20 calendar: 825M shares at $70–$78 (~$61B at the range, ~$1.2T market cap), pricing expected Wed, Nov 18 and trading Thu, Nov 19 on Nasdaq, plus a $26B private placement from AMD, Broadcom, Google, Micron, Microsoft, Nvidia and TSMC; the date is not final until pricing. After that the calendar is thin: Football Manager SPAC ($100M) and Tracx Logis (~$20M) are listed for Thanksgiving week and Primagrove slipped to Nov 30, all unconfirmed. Last week Rezera postponed its $200M IPO (it did not price), while Windward Bio (WWB) priced at $17 and closed +67.6% and vVardis (VVVV) priced at $18, below its $21–$24 range, and fell 8.3%. New filings: American Barrick Gold (ABGC, NYSE; Renaissance says over $5B possible in December) and SPACs Research Alliance V and ZA Acquisition I.",
  "highlights": [
    {
      "text": "Anthropic (ANT) set terms: 825M shares at $70–$78, expected to price Nov 18 and trade on Nasdaq Nov 19",
      "unconfirmed": false,
      "note": "Registration not yet effective; the date isn't final until pricing"
    },
    {
      "text": "Windward Bio (WWB) priced at $17 and closed its Nov 13 debut up 67.6%",
      "unconfirmed": false
    },
    {
      "text": "vVardis (VVVV) priced at $18, below its $21–$24 range, and closed down 8.3% on Nov 13",
      "unconfirmed": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Rezera (RZRA) postponed its $200M IPO on market conditions; it did not price",
      "unconfirmed": false
    },
    {
      "text": "American Barrick Gold (ABGC) filed an S-1 for an NYSE IPO; Renaissance says it could raise over $5B in December",
      "unconfirmed": true,
      "note": "No terms set; size and timing are Renaissance's estimate"
    }
  ],
